    "done_when": "Per §83 of the plan: the follower's stream prints a line only for the six actionable kinds the section lists, each once when it becomes true, as that run's own row; the needs-you summary line and its reminder cadence are gone; launches, working/waiting changes, the coordinator's own merge or discard, re-arm baseline rows and reload notices leave the stream and still appear in crew view. tests/test_the_stream_carries_only_actionable_lines.py drives the follower over a stream with one event of every kind and finds a line for exactly the six actionable kinds, each once; a delivered run prints its row once and never a needs-you line; a twelve-item outstanding set held 35 minutes prints nothing more. Every test file under tests/ importing reckon.crew.ticker, reckon.crew.needs_you or reckon.crew_follow_commands, rebuilt from the head tree, adds no failure against a base arm, both arms from git checkouts under the run's own scratch directory with RECKON_SESSION_HOST_SETTLE, RECKON_FOLLOWER_OWNER, RECKON_FOLLOWER_IMAGE_COMMIT and RECKON_FOLLOWER_SOURCE_ROOT unset, run in place on the fleet node with pytest -n 8; any id failing in one arm only is run five times alone in each arm. If a test outside the write paths fails because it asserts a line or row this section removes, stop with status blocked and name its failure id so the coordinator can widen. tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py passes at head. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT=. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the changed files, judged against the base blobs.",
